{
  "description": "Grid-frequency window rule for the drand-quicknet+elexon-freq-v1 tag: raw Elexon FREQ bodies and the freq_value of the window starting at freq_start, or why the window is invalid. The rows are body.data, decoded keeping each JSON number's exact text (never through a float).",
  "rules": [
    "A row that is not a JSON object is ignored.",
    "A body with the same key twice in one object, at any depth (keys compared after unescaping), is invalid with reason duplicate_key, before any row is read: readers that keep the first or the last value would get different windows from the same bytes.",
    "An object row belongs to a reading time when its measurementTime is exactly YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ for that time; other object rows are ignored.",
    "Every matching object row counts: one gives the reading (a missing, null, quoted or malformed frequency invalidates the window); two or more are a duplicate.",
    "A reading is the JSON number text as whole mHz: digits, at most 3 decimal places padded with zeros, no exponent, sign or leading zero; 0 is a zero reading; it must be in [47000, 52999].",
    "8 readings 15 s apart from freq_start, in time order, joined by ';'. A run of 6 or more identical readings is stuck.",
    "invalid.reason (and invalid.at, the reading time) is the first failure in time order, then stuck; duplicate_key has no at. A verifier must refuse every invalid case and may report its own reason."
  ],
